  "answer": "This feature request has been filed before. Tickets #33337, #39249 and #40443 all ask for PowerToys to emulate horizontal scrolling by holding a modifier key (Shift, Ctrl or a user-chosen key) while using the normal vertical mouse wheel. #40443 was closed as a duplicate of #33337, and #39249 was closed as a duplicate of #1153, which was not shown to me and is the original request. No implementation has been announced in these tickets. Please add a thumbs-up and any extra use cases to the original request instead of keeping this ticket open. In the meantime, many apps already support Shift+scroll for horizontal scrolling, and Excel supports Ctrl+Shift+scroll. Word does not respond to Shift+scroll. Per #24731, that is app behavior rather than a PowerToys problem, and a mouse with a tilt or thumb wheel does work in Word."
